    <name>SilverScreen</name>
    <summary>Native YouTube client that plays videos with MPV</summary>
    <description>
        <p>
            SilverScreen is a native YouTube client for GNOME, built with GTK 4 and
            Libadwaita. Search YouTube or paste a video link, then play it through a
            built-in libmpv player or an external MPV install, with stream extraction
            handled by yt-dlp.
        </p>
        <p>Supports both Wayland and X11 sessions through GTK 4.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Search YouTube and open results directly in MPV</li>
            <li>Optional sign-in for Home recommendations, subscriptions, and history</li>
            <li>Queue, comments, ratings, SponsorBlock skipping, and Discord Rich Presence</li>
        </ul>
    </description>
